This is a Jekyll + Chirpy (gem) blog, not a React/Tailwind app.

When changing UI:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/weo0o0-jekyll-ui/SKILL.md` and apply `impeccable`, `web-design-guidelines`, `frontend-design`, `check-fix-accessibility` as relevant.
2. Put visual tokens and styles in `assets/css/weo0o0.css`, behavior in `assets/js/weo0o0-motion.js`, head wiring in `_includes/metadata-hook.html`. Only override a Chirpy layout/include when CSS cannot do it, copied from the installed gem version.
3. Keep Catppuccin Mocha surfaces (`#1e1e2e` base, `#cdd6f4` text) and brand teal `#00adb5`. Pair Gowun Batang (reading) with Gowun Dodum (UI) and Pretendard fallback.
4. Preserve dark mode, `:focus-visible`, and `prefers-reduced-motion` rules. Keep post URLs `/:categories/:title/`.
5. Verify with `npm run pa11y:home` / `npm run pa11y:ci` when a local Jekyll server is available.
